==Trivia== 
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls]. 
**In the Italian and Japanese language setting of the game, the Dart Goblin's name translates to "Blowgun Goblin". In the French, German, Spanish, Dutch, Norwegian. Arabic, Persian, Malaysian, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Dart Goblin's name translates to "Blowpipe Goblin", "Blowgun Kobold", "Dart-throwing Duende", "Blowpipe Kobold", "Blowing Goblin", "Arrow-blowing Ghoul", "Blow Dart Goblin", "Greedy Goblin", and "Dart-throwing Leprechauns" respectively.
**The Dart Goblin is 1 of 6 evolved [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Mortar/Evolution|Mortar]], [[Goblin Cage/Evolution|Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Giant/Evolution|Goblin Giant]], [[Goblin Barrel/Evolution|Goblin Barrel]], and [[Goblin Drill/Evolution|Goblin Drill]].
*The Dart Goblin's Evolution might be based off the [[Buff#Poison Attack|Poison Attack]] [[buff]] that the Dart Goblin has been featured with in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|10/6/2024 Goblin Buffs Challenge]].
*The poison clouds change color depending on the number of darts hit on the target. The first stage has a blue color, the second stage changes to a purple color, and the third stage changes to an orange color. In addition, skulls appear after the second stage.
*The Dart Goblin’s Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*The Evolved Dart Goblin was created when a Dart Goblin fell into a [[Miner]]'s tunnel and stumbled upon a poisonous mask in a Goblin temple, as seen in a [https://www.youtube.com/shorts/LU877q6R8k4 short].

